  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are clear this morning with\nnothing on radar as the weather pattern remains on the dry and\nquiet side.\n\nAll models are depicting slowly increasing heights across northern\nand central nevada through Friday as an east Pacific upper level\nridge slides eastward during this timeframe. This will result in a\ncontinuation of the dry and quiet weather over the forecast area.\nThe ridge axis appears to be at its maximum on Friday, which will\nlead to very warm temperatures for the area. In fact some locales\nmay see near record temperatures. Winds will be light around 5-10\nmph with gusts up to 20 mph each afternoon.\n\nBy the start of next week, models show slight cooling as a weak\nupper level trough moves over the western United States that will\nhelp weaken the upper ridge. However, look for conditions to \nremain dry with above normal temperatures continuing.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence for dry weather\nconditions over the next 7 days. High confidence for warming\ntemperature trend, becoming unseasonably warm over the weekend\nwith above normal temperatures. Low to moderate confidence on\ncooler temperatures next week from a weak upper level trough. No \nchanges to NBM grids at this time.",
